{"availability":"available","full":"kouhxp/textsnap","name":"textsnap","description":"Snap any image, screenshot, or webpage into plaintext. No GPU. No cloud. One command.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":190,"forks":8,"created":"2026-05-24T13:57:05Z","updated":"2026-09-29T17:46:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["image2text","ocr","onnx","paddlepaddle","screenshot","transcription"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":190,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Snap any image, screenshot, or webpage into plaintext. No GPU. No cloud. One command.","That's it. You get a .txt next to your shell, recognized on your CPU, from a screenshot, a photo, an image URL, or even a webpage."],"features":["⚡ Fast by default, smart when it matters. Every image first goes through PP-OCRv6 medium (34.5M parameters, 140 MB of ONNX): text detection plus line recognition, a small fraction of the VLM's compute. If the result…","🧾 Structure on request. --structured goes straight to the VLM and keeps its native markdown: tables, headings, document structure.","🖥 Runs on CPU. Both engines run on ONNX Runtime with plain old cores, pinned to your physical-core count. No CUDA. No M-series-only tricks.","🖼 Images, screenshots, URLs, webpages. Point it at a local file, a direct image URL, or a full article URL — it isolates the main content and OCRs the most prominent image. Or OCR straight from your clipboard with no…","📴 Offline after first run. 140 MB downloads on first use; the 1.1 GB VLM only the first time a page needs it (or you ask for --structured). Both stay cached. No API keys. No quotas. Your images never leave your machine."],"sourceUrl"